      "content": "That makes sense. The \"micro-feedback\" idea is good.\n\nI'm trying to explain the *nature* of these disruptions to my director, though. It's hard to call them \"performance issues\" because they aren't big enough for HR to act on, but they are just... irritating. They feel almost mischievous, like someone is intentionally pulling small threads to see the whole thing unravel. \n\nSince you use a lot of descriptive language, do you have any good metaphors or archetypes I could use to describe these kinds of \"small, sneaky, disruptive\" behaviors? I want to convey that they are subtle but destructive without sounding like I'm just complaining about personalities.",
